d 'QREGARK': module for quantile regression with AR(k) errors, by Prais-Winsten or Cochrane-Orcutt estimation.
d
d  qregark fits a linear quantile regression model with
d autoregressive errors of order k. The regression coefficients b
d and the AR coefficients rho_1,...,rho_k are estimated jointly by
d minimizing the quantile check function. qregark extends qreg to
d AR(k) errors in the same way that prais extends regress.  By
d default, qregark uses a Prais-Winsten-type estimator, which also
d uses the first k observations of each time segment, transformed
d by the stationary covariance of the errors (Prais and Winsten
d 1954; Vougas 2021; Dielman and Rose 1994). With option corc,
d qregark uses the conditional (Cochrane-Orcutt-type) estimator of
d Tian et al. (2018), which conditions on the first k observations
d of each segment. 
d
d KW: quantile regression
d KW: autocorrelation
d KW: Prais-Winsten
d KW: Cochrane-Orcutt
d KW: time series
d
d Requires: Stata version 13
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261125
d
d Author: Ariel Linden, Linden Consulting Group, LLC
d Support: email alinden@@lindenconsulting.org
d
